VALUES (4400093516010125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to multimedia in the context of Unit 1. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Basics of Image editing in the context of Unit 2. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Different Image editing tools-Selection tools in the context of Unit 3. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to Animations in the context of Unit 4. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to multimedia appears in “Unit 1”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to concept of graphics-bitmap images, vector graphics, Color channels, Bit depth, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to concept of graphics-bitmap images; vector graphics; Color channels; Bit depth. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Basics of Image editing appears in “Unit 2”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to the Image editing interface, need of image editing, create documents(new, save different format, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to the Image editing interface; need of image editing; create documents(new; save different format. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Different Image editing tools-Selection tools appears in “Unit 3”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to Crop and slice tools, Measuring tools, retouching tool, painting tools, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to Crop and slice tools; Measuring tools; retouching tool; painting tools. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Animations appears in “Unit 4”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to software Interface- Start page, Creating custom workspace layouts, import formats, keyboard shortcuts, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to software Interface-