VALUES (4400093516010134, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction to multimedia in Multimedia and Animation Tools. Explain the governing principle, justify your method, and include a check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Basics of Image editing in Multimedia and Animation Tools. Explain the governing principle, justify your method, and include a check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Working with layers in Multimedia and Animation Tools. Explain the governing principle, justify your method, and include a check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction to actionscript in Multimedia and Animation Tools. Explain the governing principle, justify your method, and include a check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to multimedia appears in “Unit 1”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to concept of graphics-bitmap images, vector graphics, Color channels, Bit depth, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to concept of graphics-bitmap images; vector graphics; Color channels; Bit depth. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Basics of Image editing appears in “Unit 2”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to the Image editing interface, need of image editing, create documents(new, save different format, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to the Image editing interface; need of image editing; create documents(new; save different format. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Layers keep image or animation elements separately editable and can be shown, hidden, reordered or composited without flattening all content.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to properties of layers; renaming layers; grouping of layers; guide layer. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning/purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to actionscript appears in “Unit 6”. Define its role, explain the main components or steps, connect it to navigating actionpanel, different actions – stop(), play(), navigating between frames, provide a practical example, and note a verification step or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept logically and relate it to navigating actionpanel; different actions – stop(); play(); navigating between frames. State relevant rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Multimedia and Animation Tools task. Identify the objective, method and expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the outcome against the requirement, mention a limitation or error source, and justify the selection.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

